# ---- preserved evidence: on disk only, never in the repository ----
# The Mac PPC decompile corpus, the retail PC binary, the SDK source, the oracle
# goldens/savegame corpus, the preservation set and the captured device logs are
# the primary evidence for every reverse-engineering claim.  They are retail-derived
# and are never published, so the whole tree stays untracked.
docs/evidence/
logs/

# the oracle runtime corpora (goldens, saves, captures, the GL1 export, build and
# wine prefix) are retail-derived evidence: kept on disk, never tracked.  The
# oracle's own specs and tools inside docs/oracle/ stay tracked.
docs/oracle/

# ---- IDA databases: regenerable caches, never committed ----
*.id0
*.id1
*.id2
*.idb
*.i64
*.nam
*.til

# ---- ephemeral ----
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store

# ---- process and provenance material: on disk only, never in the repository ----
personal/

